WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.240
 With your RStudio Cloud account, 
  you'll have access to your own 

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.400
 personal workspace, as well as the ability 
  to create additional workspaces. 

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.360
 As an educator, you might find it 
  helpful to create 

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.600
 a single workspace 
  for each of your classes or workshops. 

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.520
 This creates a shared space 
  for all of the learners within a class, 

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.800
 allowing you to create 
  and share assignments with your learners, 

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.040
 as well as provide learners with a place 
  to complete their coursework. 

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.800
 What's more, you can view 
  the work of your learners 

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.840
 by going into their RStudio projects. 

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.800
 Once we log into RStudio Cloud,  

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.200
 navigate to the menu on the left 
  by clicking here. 

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.120
 We can also choose to keep this menu open 
  by clicking on this pin. 

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.240
 Here we see my personal workspace, as well 

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.160
 as a series of workspaces 
  that I've created or joined. 

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.080
 We can create a new workspace 
  by clicking on this new space button 

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.120
 and naming our new workspace.  

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.320
 For the purposes of this example, 
  I'll call our workspace Fall 

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.800
 2021 Data Visualization. 

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:02.840
 Once we're in the  

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.800
 workspace for a course, 
  we can create projects, add co-teachers 

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.760
 and teaching assistants, as well as add 
  learners and change access permissions . 

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.040
 These are all topics 
  covered in additional videos, 

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.880
 and I encourage you to check out 
  our RStudio Cloud playlist to learn more. 

